= Solution
{parent=3}

For $\theta>0$, the <exponential martingale for Brownian motion> and the <Doob maximal inequality for a nonnegative submartingale> give
$$
\mathbb P\left(\sup_{t\leq s}B_t\geq a\right)
\leq\exp\left(-\theta a+\frac12\theta^2s\right).
$$
Taking $\theta=a/s$ gives $e^{-a^2/(2s)}$. Apply the same argument to $-B$ and use the <union bound>:
$$
\boxed{\mathbb P\left(\sup_{t\leq s}|B_t|\geq a\right)
\leq2e^{-a^2/(2s)}.}
$$

